{#- State template of the UI helper "Arbeitspreis aktuell" (Template → Sensor,
    sensor.electricity_work_price, unit EUR/kWh, state class measurement, not
    exposed to Assist). The energy dashboard prices the grid import with it,
    so Home Assistant records the cost of every hour at the price valid then.

    Three tariff slots, each with input_datetime.electricity_tariff_N_valid_from
    (date only), input_number.electricity_tariff_N_work_price (ct/kWh) and
    input_number.electricity_tariff_N_base_price (EUR per month). The active
    slot is the one with the latest date that is not after today; a slot with
    a work price of 0 is unused. The price changes at local midnight.
    docs/smart_meter.md, section "Tariff". -#}
{%- set ns = namespace(start='', value=none) -%}
{%- set today = now().date() | string -%}
{%- for i in range(1, 4) -%}
  {%- set start = states('input_datetime.electricity_tariff_' ~ i ~ '_valid_from') -%}
  {%- set work = states('input_number.electricity_tariff_' ~ i ~ '_work_price') | float(0) -%}
  {%- if work > 0 and start is match('[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$') and start <= today and start > ns.start -%}
    {%- set ns.start = start -%}
    {%- set ns.value = work / 100 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{ (ns.value | round(5)) if ns.value is not none else none }}
